# Applied to the upload of EVERY Vercel project built from this repository,
# immediately after the clone and before any Root Directory setting is resolved.
# Both the Go API project and the web app project deploy from here, so anything
# excluded is excluded for both.
#
# EVERY PATTERN MUST BE ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH. These are gitignore
# patterns: an unanchored `docs/` matched a directory named docs at ANY depth,
# so it also deleted web/content/docs/ — the entire documentation — from the
# upload, and the deployed site served 404s for every /docs page while the rest
# of the app worked. Anchor, or it will happen again to config/ or proto/.
#
# For the same reason src/web/ is not listed at all: excluding it removed the
# app the web project exists to build. Carrying it in the API project's upload
# costs a little transfer and nothing else.
#
# The Hugo tree that /docs/ used to exclude is gone; the documentation now lives
# in src/web/content/docs/ and must ship.
#
# The dataset under dataset/ is not needed by either build and is not excluded
# either. Neither claim it carried before was right for long: it was compiled in
# with go:embed, then "read at runtime from the filesystem" — which took
# production down, because Vercel's Go builder ships the compiled binary and
# nothing else, so these files reach the BUILD and never the function. The
# deployed server now fetches the records over HTTP from the commit it was built
# from. Left in the upload because the transfer is cheap and a whole-tree
# exclusion is a sharper tool than the saving justifies; nothing depends on it
# being here, and verify-deploy-upload.sh no longer claims anything does.
/src/api/proto/
/.sources/
/src/builder/
/coverage.out
